{
  "about": "Where Verse's earn loop (tools/earn.mjs) finds errors people hit and will pay to have fixed: official documentation only, never a forum or a third-party blog. kind code: an index links one page per error and the error is the code in the link. kind headings: the listed pages (and, with index and link, the pages an index links to) have the error messages as their headings. A candidate ships only when its error text is found word for word on the official page it cites, and never when a page already covers it. weight is Verse's prior for how likely a person hitting this platform's errors pays for a fix (Make and n8n users run business automations; a Vercel or Cloudflare error is often a developer's own to fix); the loop multiplies it by what each platform's pages earn and get pressed (domains/earnings-log.json weights).",
  "sources": [
